4. LinuxCNC
   License:   LGPL v3 / GPL v2 (mixed)
   Source:    https://github.com/LinuxCNC/linuxcnc
   Website:   https://linuxcnc.org

   This project uses LinuxCNC's Python bindings and runs as a
   companion application alongside LinuxCNC. It is not a derivative
   of LinuxCNC itself.

   Additionally bundled from the LinuxCNC source tree:
   - scripts/kins_oracle/trtfuncs.c and kins_util.c (v2.9.4, GPL v2) —
     vendored VERBATIM as the compiled test oracle for the viewer's
     xyzac/xyzbc-trt kinematics mirrors (see scripts/kins_oracle/README.md)
   - examples/sim_config/machine-xyzac/ STL geometry — generated by
     scripts/vismach_to_stl.py from LinuxCNC's vismach xyzac-trt-gui
     sample (GPL v2+, Rudy du Preez)
   - examples/sim_config/remap_subs/ — adapted from the LinuxCNC 2.9.4
     table-rotary-tilting sample config's switchkins remaps (GPL v2+)
   - scripts/kins_oracle/xyzacb_trsrn.comp (LinuxCNC master, GPL v2,
     David Mueller) — vendored VERBATIM as the compiled test oracle for
     the TWP machine's switchable kinematics (identity/TCP/TOOL-plane;
     see scripts/kins_oracle/README.md). Uses master's handle-style HAL
     pin API, so it is compiled against stubs by the harness and CANNOT
     be halcompile'd on 2.9.
     (The TWP product itself — the examples/sim_config/twp/ remap fork,
     its installable xyzacb_trsrn.comp copy, and the
     machine-xyzacb-trsrn/ viewer model — lives on the feat/twp branch;
     that branch's NOTICE carries their attributions.)


